from (values
('127.105.d.4.N',3,'A designer checks that the inside layout and outside appearance are:','["Opposites", "Ignored", "Unrelated", "Compatible"]'::jsonb,3,'Interior and exterior should work together.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.N',4,'The size and location of windows should match both interior needs and:','["The exterior elevation design", "The phone plan", "The car", "The paint can"]'::jsonb,0,'Windows serve inside and out.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.O',3,'Schematic drawings are:','["Bills", "Early, simple drawings showing the overall design", "Tax forms", "Final construction details"]'::jsonb,1,'Schematics show concepts.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.O',4,'Which set includes plans, elevations, and sections?','["Bank forms", "Calendars", "Schematic drawings", "Menus"]'::jsonb,2,'Typical schematic set.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.P',3,'Scaled wall thickness drawings show walls drawn with:','["Single lines only", "No width", "Random width", "Their actual thickness to scale"]'::jsonb,3,'Poche shows wall thickness.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.P',4,'A wall section drawing cuts through a wall to show its:','["Layers and materials", "Owner", "Color", "Address"]'::jsonb,0,'Sections reveal layers.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.Q',3,'A detail drawing is used to explain:','["The weather", "How parts of a floor or wall are assembled", "The rent", "Parking"]'::jsonb,1,'Details show construction.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.Q',4,'Details are drawn at a larger scale than plans so that:','["Walls vanish", "Dimensions disappear", "Small connections can be read clearly", "Less paper is used"]'::jsonb,2,'Larger scale shows small parts.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.R',3,'The Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) requires buildings to:','["Exclude visitors", "Be painted white", "Have no doors", "Be accessible to people with disabilities"]'::jsonb,3,'ADA sets accessibility.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.R',4,'An ADA-compliant ramp includes a gentle slope and:','["Handrails and landings", "Gravel", "Steps only", "No edge"]'::jsonb,0,'Ramps need rails and landings.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.S',3,'Assembling a design in three dimensions helps a designer to:','["Shorten plans", "See how the parts fit together", "Remove parts", "Avoid review"]'::jsonb,1,'3D models show relationships.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.S',4,'A physical or digital 3D model allows clients to understand a design more:','["Vaguely", "Slowly", "Easily than from plans alone", "Poorly"]'::jsonb,2,'Models communicate.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.T',3,'Customizing screen menus in CAD software lets a user to:','["Slow down", "Hide tools", "Delete drawings", "Reach common commands faster"]'::jsonb,3,'Customization saves time.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.T',4,'A drafter creates a custom toolbar for frequently used wall commands. This is:','["Menu customization", "File deletion", "Plotting", "System repair"]'::jsonb,0,'Custom menus speed work.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.U',3,'In CAD, a line is defined by two:','["Printers", "Points", "Colors", "Layers"]'::jsonb,1,'Lines connect points.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.U',4,'Coordinates such as 4,6 place a point by its:','["Layer name", "Scale", "X and Y values", "Pen color"]'::jsonb,2,'Coordinate pairs locate a point.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.V',3,'A one-point perspective has how many vanishing points?','["Two", "Three", "Zero", "One"]'::jsonb,3,'One-point has a single vanishing point.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.V',4,'In a freehand one-point perspective of a hallway, the lines of the walls meet at the:','["Vanishing point", "Page margin", "Title block", "Scale bar"]'::jsonb,0,'Lines converge.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.W',3,'A bill of materials lists the:','["Workers'' birthdays", "Items and quantities needed", "Clients", "Weather"]'::jsonb,1,'BOMs list materials.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.W',4,'Software can create a bill of materials by counting:','["Phone numbers", "Employees", "Drawing objects such as doors and windows", "Coffee cups"]'::jsonb,2,'CAD data feeds BOMs.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.X',3,'To change an existing CAD drawing, a drafter uses commands such as move, copy, and:','["Park", "Cook", "Sing", "Trim"]'::jsonb,3,'Edit commands modify drawings.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.X',4,'Putting walls, doors, and dimensions on separate layers makes a drawing easier to:','["Edit and control", "Lose", "Delete", "Print blank"]'::jsonb,0,'Layers organize drawings.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.Y',3,'Plotting a drawing means:','["Coloring it", "Printing it to scale on paper", "Deleting it", "Writing about it"]'::jsonb,1,'Plots produce hard copies.','original'),
('127.105.d.4.Y',4,'Before plotting a floor plan at 1/4 inch = 1 foot, a drafter must check the:','["Weather", "Phone", "Plot scale and sheet size", "Chair"]'::jsonb,2,'Plot settings matter.','original'),
('127.105.d.5.A',3,'Drawing a building from direct observation helps develop:','["Typing skill", "Cooking skill", "Math only", "Visual perception and sketching skill"]'::jsonb,3,'Observation trains the eye.','original'),
('127.105.d.5.A',4,'A student sketching the front of a school building is practicing:','["Illustrating ideas from observation", "Plotting", "Surveying only", "Estimating"]'::jsonb,0,'Sketching observed forms.','original'),
('127.105.d.5.B',3,'Columns, arches, and domes are examples of architectural:','["Taxes", "Elements", "Habits", "Titles"]'::jsonb,1,'Elements form buildings.','original'),
('127.105.d.5.B',4,'Comparing a Roman arch with a pointed Gothic arch is an exercise in:','["Zoning", "Plotting", "Contrasting architectural elements", "Estimating costs"]'::jsonb,2,'Compare and contrast forms.','original'),
('127.105.d.6.A',3,'Elaborating on a sketch of a building adds:','["Erasures only", "Confusion", "Blank space", "Detail and refinement"]'::jsonb,3,'Elaboration refines ideas.','original'),
